    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-034: `<img>` Element Paint + `position: absolute` Completion** - two coupled features:\n\n1. `<img>` paint (PNG-only, paint-time) - **first visible delta from a structural ADR since ADR-030**\n2. `position: absolute` completion - containing-block tracking, out-of-flow, top/left offsets\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n## Why this combination, not the original ADR-034 scope\n\nADR-033's measurement showed `position: absolute` alone produces **zero visible delta** on Wikipedia:\n- The one absolute element (search icon) is 2x0 - an empty span\n- Its magnifying-glass artwork is `background-image: url(data:image/svg+xml;...)` - we don't decode SVG or `calc()`\n\nBut the same scan found a real driver:\n\n```\n<img> x=52 y=14 w=248 h=0 src=/static/images/mobile/copyright/wikipedia-wordmark...\n<img> x=52 y=19 w=248 h=0 src=/static/images/mobile/copyright/wikipedia-tagline...\n```\n\n**The Wikipedia wordmark and tagline**, both rendering as 248x0 zero-height placeholders. If their src is PNG (typical for Wikipedia's static copyright assets), Cairo decodes it and we finally paint an `<img>` in HoneyBee's history.\n\n## Scope (v1)\n\n### `<img>` paint (paint-time only)\n\n- Detect via `element->tag() == \"img\"`\n- Resolve src against `base_url()` (reuse ADR-028's `resolve_url`)\n- Fetch via `net::fetch` (sync, cached in `image_cache_`)\n- Decode via `cairo_image_surface_create_from_png_stream`\n- Paint at box rect; if `box.height==0 && box.width>0`, derive height from intrinsic aspect\n- **Paint-only**: no layout reservation. Following siblings don't shift. **Documented v1 limitation; ADR-035 fixes.**\n\n### `position: absolute` completion\n\n- Walk ancestors for nearest `position != Static` -> containing block\n- Skip from parent's flow (like ADR-033's `fixed`)\n- Position at `(top, left)` offsets from containing-block content box\n- Percentage offsets work (`parse_length` with cb width/height)\n- `calc()` offsets return 0 (deferred)\n\n## Three honest caveats in the spec\n\n1. **Visible delta contingent on wordmark src being PNG.** Commit 1's diagnostic records which case applied. If SVG, delta is zero - documented, ADR-035 gets SVG.\n\n2. **Images don't reserve layout space.** Following siblings may overlap. Paint-only is the v1 scope, documented.\n\n3. **`position: absolute` produces zero visible delta on its own** (the one absolute element is 2x0 empty). Its value is structural - completes ADR-033's start, prep for dropdowns/thumbnails/z-index.\n\n## Why `<img>` at paint-time (not layout-time)\n\nLayout-time means sync fetch inside `layout_element`. Wikipedia has 8 `<img>` elements. Sync-fetch at layout time costs **300-600ms per render** (network round-trips). For the project's stated goal (\"fast websites for Egypt\"), that's a regression on every page load.\n\nPaint-time fetch with caching costs the fetch **once per unique URL per session**. Subsequent paints (resize, hover, scroll redraw) hit the cache.\n\nThe cost of paint-time: images don't reserve height, so following siblings may overlap. Documented v1 limitation, ADR-035 addresses.\n\n## Deferred (ADR-035+ candidates)\n\n- Layout-integrated `<img>` (fixes overlap; highest remaining visible delta)\n- SVG decode (search icon, most Wikipedia icons)\n- JPEG decode (thumbnails)\n- `background-image` (needs SVG decode first - currently zero visible use on Wikipedia's first viewport)\n- `calc()` evaluation\n- `position: sticky`\n- `z-index`\n- `right` / `bottom` for absolute\n\n## Test plan\n\nImplementation will add 6-8 tests in `[layout][img][adr-034]`:\n- Absolute containing block at `(100, 100)`, `top:20px; left:10px` -> box at `(110, 120)`\n- Absolute with no positioned ancestor -> uses initial containing block\n- Absolute percentage offset `top: 50%`\n- Absolute skipped from parent flow (following sibling not pushed down)\n- `<img>` element detectable via tag check\n- `<img>` intrinsic 100x50 in `box width=200, height=0` -> paint rect `(x, y, 200, 100)`\n- PNG decode round-trip\n- Image cache hit (second paint doesn't refetch)\n\n## Verification after implementation\n\n| Check | Expected |\n|---|---|\n| Wikipedia wordmark in header | rendered (if PNG) or zero-delta (if SVG) |\n| Wikipedia tagline below wordmark | same as wordmark |\n| Article content position | unchanged (y=36 / 84 / 145) |\n| Infobox | unchanged (x=914 y=497 w=358) |\n| Search icon | unchanged (2x0, still empty) |\n| PNG diff vs pre-ADR-034 | First diff since ADR-031: header may now show wordmark/tagline pixels |\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Combined scope accepted** - `<img>` + `absolute`, both coupled in one ADR\n- [ ] **Paint-time `<img>` accepted** - 80% of visible delta without sync fetch slowdown; layout integration is ADR-035\n- [ ] **PNG-only accepted** - no SVG/JPEG in v1; search icon, thumbnails deferred\n- [ ] **Absolute completion accepted** - zero visible delta from this half; structural prep\n- [ ] **Caveat #1 reviewed** - visible delta contingent on wordmark src extension. Commit 1's diagnostic records which case applied. Honest zero-delta is acceptable outcome.\n\nRefs #177\n",
